      {
        "id": "plan-data-model",
        "kind": "plan",
        "title": "Data model",
        "text": "- A new `stock_reservation` row per order line per warehouse, referencing `stock_level (warehouse_id, sku)`.\n- `stock_level.reserved` holds the reserved quantity. Available stock is `on_hand - reserved`; checkout never writes `on_hand`.\n- Migration 002 only adds; old code keeps working against the new schema.",
        "path": "plan.md",
        "section": "Data model"
      },
      {
        "id": "ledger-departures",
        "kind": "plan",
        "title": "Departures",
        "text": "- Added `stock_level.version` for optimistic concurrency with the WMS sync. The plan's conditional update alone was not enough once a second writer exists.\n- Dropped the proposed `released_at` column. `status` plus `created_at` and `expires_at` answer every question we had, and `expired` is now a status of its own instead of a kind of release.",
        "path": "ledger.md",
        "section": "Departures"
      },
      {
        "id": "ledger-outcome",
        "kind": "plan",
        "title": "Outcome",
        "text": "Complete on 2026-09-24. All completion checks pass, shop#41 and shop#44 are merged, and the flag is on for all traffic.\nFollow-up outside this work: the as-built capture shows `stock_reservation.id` as nullable. SQLite lets a non-integer primary key hold NULL unless it is declared `NOT NULL`. Tracked as shop#47 and recorded in [inventory schema notes](../../knowledge/shop/inventory-schema.md).",
        "path": "ledger.md",
        "section": "Outcome"
      }
    ],
